          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            5. Do Premier Protein Flavors Have Different Nutrition Labels?
          </h2>

          <p>
            Yes, but only slightly within the Classic line: every Classic flavor lists 30 g of protein, 160 calories, 3 g of fat, 1 g of sugar and 0 g of added sugar per shake, per Premier's labels at the time of writing. The differences are in sodium, fiber and carbohydrate, and they come from the flavoring, not from a different base.
          </p>

          <p>
            Sodium varies most. Chocolate and Strawberries & Cream list 230 mg per 11.5 oz shake and Cookies & Cream 220 mg, while Caramel lists 350 mg, Cake Batter 370 mg and Chocolate Peanut Butter 380 mg. That gap of about 150 mg is small against a 2,300 mg daily limit, but it adds up if you drink two or three shakes a day on a sodium-restricted diet.
          </p>

          <p>
            Fiber and carbohydrate move a little too. Chocolate lists 2 g of fiber and 4 g of carbohydrate, Chocolate Peanut Butter 3 g of fiber and 6 g of carbohydrate, and Caramel and Vanilla list 0 g of fiber with 2 to 3 g of carbohydrate. None of these numbers changes much for most people, but the chocolate flavors are the better pick if you want a little fiber with your protein.
