        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Caramel is the best Premier Protein flavor for most buyers: it is the only flavor that finished in the top five of three of the four published rankings we compared, it has no caffeine and, like every Classic shake, it lists 30 g of protein, 160 calories and 0 g of added sugar per Premier's label. Chocolate is the classic if you like a milder drink, and Café Latte or Caramel Macchiato is the pick if your shake doubles as your morning coffee.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Before you buy a case, check three things on the label: caffeine in the coffee flavors, 2 g of added sugar in the Indulgence line, and sodium, which varies by about 150 mg between flavors. Try untested flavors in a 4-pack, and if you drink Premier every day, the Vanilla or Chocolate Milkshake powder is the cheapest way to get the same flavor per gram of protein. For other brands, see our <a href="/best-protein-drink/">best protein drink</a> rankings.
          </p>
